    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1983217592958611531",
      "url": "https://x.com/IPRTelangana/status/1983217592958611531",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/IPRTelangana/status/1983217592958611531",
      "text": "𝗧𝗥𝗔𝗙𝗙𝗜𝗖 𝗔𝗗𝗩𝗜𝗦𝗢𝗥𝗬\n\nTraffic Diversions in Connection with Construction of the Elevated Corridor from Paradise Junction to Dairy Farm Road (NH-44)\n\nIn view of the commencement of construction of the Elevated Corridor from Paradise Junction to Dairy Farm Road on NH-44, the following road closures and traffic diversions will be implemented from 30.10.2025 for a period of approximately nine (09) months.\n\n🛑 Road Closure:\n\nThe road stretch between Rajiv Gandhi Statue Junction and Balamrai, in both directions, will remain closed during the construction period.\n\nCommuters are advised to avoid the route between Balamrai and CTO Junction, as traffic congestion is expected on adjoining roads and junctions.\n\n🔁 Diversion Points / Alternate Routes:\n\nFrom Balanagar towards Panjagutta / Tank Bund:\n→ Tadbund → Mastan Café → Diamond Point → Right Turn → Mudfort → NCC → JBS → SBI\n\nFrom Suchitra towards Panjagutta / Tank Bund:\n→ Safe Express → Left Turn → Bapuji Nagar → Centre Point → Diamond Point → Mudfort → NCC → JBS → SBI\n\nFrom Tank Bund / Rani Gunj / Panjagutta / Rasoolpura / Plaza towards Tadbund:\n→ Divert at Rajiv Gandhi Statue Junction → Anna Nagar → Balamrai → Tadbund\n\nFor Residents of Anna Nagar:\n→ Use internal bylanes (Meeting Point bylane, Hockey Ground bylane, L&O Police Station bylane) to reach destinations without taking the route towards Rajiv Gandhi Statue Junction.\n→ Alternatively, proceed via Balamrai.\n\nFor travel assistance or emergencies, please contact  Traffic Helpline: 9010203626.\n\nCitizens are requested to cooperate with the Hyderabad Traffic Police and plan their travel accordingly.",
